204	Research And Development Chemist	Solstice Consulting Group LLC	Houston, TX	Solstice Consulting Group is seeking a Research and Development (R&D) Chemist for our client located in Houston, Texas. This role is an in-office position located in East Houston on a 9/80 work schedule. · Bachelors Degree in Chemical Engineering or Chemistry and 5+ years experience required · 3+ years laboratory experience in a manufacturing environment required · Base salary of $90k - $120k DOE plus bonus opportunity and excellent benefits The R&D Chemist is a hands-on laboratory position using knowledge and experience in organic chemistry to test new processes, separations, or improvements for existing processes. A demonstrated track record of lab-based chemistry experience in synthesis/reactions and purification is required. Process optimization and/or scale-up experience is highly desired, along with hydrogenation experience. Role Responsibilities: · Practices good laboratory oversight including inventory management and documentation. · Works safely and leads efforts in maintaining a safe, organized working environment. · Ability to independently conduct sophisticated hazard reviews based on SDS, desired chemistry, and safety documents. · Detailed knowledge of organic chemistry reactions and mechanisms. · Integration of chemical concepts with laboratory data to explain results and create predictions. · Construction and modification of sophisticated laboratory setups for synthetic reactions and distillations. · Records, organizes, and performs complex analyses of data from laboratory experiments. · Creates accurate, thorough, detailed laboratory reports that include all technical and analytical information. · Searches scientific literature and intellectual property databases to find solutions to broadly defined problems. · Proactively identifies opportunities for process improvements and proposes solutions. · Performs maintenance on laboratory equipment such as: GCs, titrators, vacuum pumps, liquid pumps, flash point, boiling point range, and thermal testing apparatus. · Intermediate mechanical skills, familiarity with hand tools, and mechanical troubleshooting experience are highly desired. · Basic experience with process modeling and ability to learn details of distillation and reaction modeling. · Ability and willingness to help supervise and teach younger chemists. · Ability to clearly present data and results to broader audiences in written and verbal formats. Presentation skills are a plus. · Currently hold or have the ability to obtain a TWIC Card. Requirements: · Bachelor's degree in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering and 3+ years of relevant laboratory experience in a manufacturing environment required. Advanced degree a plus. · Detailed knowledge of organic chemistry and analytical techniques for analyzing organic mixtures is essential. Familiarity with commodity chemical production is highly desired. · Fundamental knowledge in thermodynamics, distillation, and separations. · Excellent mechanical skills to properly handle, maintain, and repair laboratory equipment. · Hands-on experience with complex laboratory apparatus such as reactors, distillation columns, and vacuum systems. · In-depth knowledge of general laboratory practices and wet chemical procedures, with a focus on organic reactions. · Solid experience and familiarity with MS Office applications, especially Word and Excel. · Ability to work independently with minimal supervision. · Ability to effectively plan lab experiments and execute work in a way that supports multiple business priorities	https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/research-and-development-chemist-at-solstice-consulting-group-llc-4406715501	linkedin_guest	httpswwwlinkedincomjobsviewresearchanddevelopmentchemistatsolsticeconsultinggroupllc440671	\N	\N		2026-05-01 12:36:59.601795+00	2026-05-01 12:36:59.602706+00	· 3+ years laboratory experience in a manufacturing environment required · Base salary of $90k - $120k DOE